<title>FRANCE: French Feb trade surplus falls to 11.37 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>French Feb trade surplus falls to 11.37 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>France had a seasonally adjusted trade surplus in February of 11.373 billion francs compared with a revised surplus in January of 11.721 billion, provisional customs office data showed.</p>
<p>The office had originally reported a surplus in January of 11.723 billion francs.  </p>
<p>Detailed figures, in billions of francs and seasonally adjusted unless otherwise stated, were as follows:</p>
<p>					    Feb    Jan</p>
<p> Trade balance			11.373  11.721</p>
<p> Trade balance (unadjusted)     11.213   6.395</p>
<p> Imports			     118.287 113.571</p>
<p> Exports			     129.660 125.292</p>
<p> Agri-business balance	     5.382   4.567</p>
<p> Energy balance		     -8.517  -7.821</p>
<p> Industrial/military balance    10.320  11.041</p>
<p> Airbus exports	     3.726 (7 planes)  3.109 (8)</p>
<p> Defence (unadj)		     0.866   0.547</p>
<p> Unadjusted exports		126.338 122.932</p>
<p> Unadjusted imports		115.125 116.537</p>
<p> European Union			7.043   7.380</p>
<p> Germany				 0.302   0.842</p>
<p> Japan				  -1.199  -1.412</p>
<p> United States			-1.933  -1.344</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
